! Proposed Definitions And Examples


!! Proposed Definition of ''cai''

;__cai__ (CAI): Attitudinal Modifier. Expresses intense emotion on the part of the speaker. Can be placed after a UI to express its intensity, or by itself to indicate that the speaker feels intensely in some unspecified emotion. Highest part of a nine point scale.  See also: sai, ru'e, cu'i, nai, pei, the preface.
** Keywords: intense emotion

!! Examples of ''cai'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''cu'i''

;__cu'i__ (CAI): Attitudinal Modifier. Expresses neutral emotion on the part of the speaker. Can be placed after a UI to express neutrality on its scale, or by itself to indicate an emotional neutrality in some unspecified emotion. Middle point of a nine point scale. See also: cai, sai, ru'e, nai, pei, the preface.
** Keywords: neutral emotion

!! Examples of ''cu'i'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''pei''

;__pei__ (CAI): Attitudinal Question. Asks the listener an emotional question. When used by itself, it asks the user to respond with a UI expressing their feelings. It can also be used in place of a CAI to ask the listener with what intensity they feel a particular emotion. See also: cai, sai, ru'e, cu'i, nai, the preface.
** Keywords: emotion ?

!! Examples of ''pei'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''ru'e''

;__ru'e__ (CAI): Attitudinal Modifier. Expresses a weak emotion on the part of the speaker. Can be placed after a UI to express its mildness, or by itself to indicate that the speaker feels weakly in some unspecified emotion. Just above the middle position of a nine-point scale. See also: cai, sai, cu'i, nai, pei, the preface.
** Keywords: weak emotion

!! Examples of ''ru'e'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''sai''

;__sai__ (CAI): Attitudinal Modifier. Expresses a strong emotion on the part of the speaker. Can be placed after a UI to express its strength, or by itself to indicate that the speaker feels strongly in some unspecified emotion. Just below the top position of a nine-point scale. See also: cai, ru'e, cu'i, nai, pei, the preface. 
** Keywords: strong emotion

!! Examples of ''sai'' Usage

! Notes


! Impact

I don't believe these definitions change the previous definitions or usage, except to expand the extant definitions.
